[model call 2026-10-11T12:56:26Z] claude-opus-5-5 (Claude Agent SDK) self-test fix turn 30: text
I edited `out/main-rA.workflow.json` in place to fix both failures, and `python3` loads it without errors. Nothing was re-run, so neither fix has been tested yet.

- **'Three wrong security answers' (5 calls to `verify_identity`, the 5th rejected): fixed.** The brief really requires this: clause 12 says three wrong answers end the check, and clause 14 says to send the customer to the app or a branch and close as `not_verified` / `failed`. The agent did say the app/branch line, but it never moved to the `identity_failed` step. When the customer offered new digits, it called `verify_identity` again and the bank refused. I added a second trigger for that move: the bank's own `wrong_answers_left` value being 0. I also added a line to the identity prompt: once the check has failed, never call `verify_identity` again, even if the customer offers a new or corrected answer. I couldn't confirm why the existing trigger didn't fire, so the new one is a backup rather than a fix of the root cause.
- **'Relative offers to pay and requests a callback' (closed as `no_callback`): fixed.** The brief really requires this: clauses 6 and 7 allow one request for another time, and a valid second offer means the callback is booked and the call closes as `not_reached` / `callback`. The first offer (Friday) was outside the window. The second (tomorrow at 18:30) was inside it, and the call to `schedule_callback` went through, but the agent then closed as `no_callback`. I changed the opening prompt to say that a valid second offer is booked too. Once `schedule_callback` has succeeded, the close reason is always `callback`; `no_callback` is only for when nothing was booked.

No other prompts, the start code node or the account post-process code were touched.

